# Approval record for the ISMS.
#
# A merge into main requires review from the owner listed here. Combined with
# branch protection this enforces approver != author, which is the evidence an
# auditor looks for under ISO/IEC 27001:2022 clause 7.5.2 (approval of
# documented information).
#
# Replace the placeholder handles below with real GitHub accounts before
# enabling branch protection. Teams (@org/team) are preferred over individuals
# so that approval does not depend on one person being available.

# Fallback: anything not matched more specifically
*                       @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners

# Data layer — changes here move the SoA and the risk picture
/data/                  @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners
/data/risks.yml         @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners
/data/soa.yml           @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners

# Automation — a change here can weaken every check
/tools/                 @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners
/.github/               @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners

# Governing documents (clause 4-10)
/docs/en/00-context/    @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners
/docs/de/00-context/    @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners
/docs/en/20-procedures/ @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners
/docs/de/20-procedures/ @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners

# Topic policies — delegate per area once owners are known, e.g.
# /docs/*/10-policies/secure-development-policy.md  @rssoftwaregmbh/engineering
/docs/en/10-policies/   @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners
/docs/de/10-policies/   @rssoftwaregmbh/isms-owners
